ining how assignment operators, augmented assignments, and expressions with substituted values are visualized. The goal is to ensure clarity in representing variable values, intermediate calculations, and the final results during code execution.\n\n\nAppending an item to the list is described, along with the updated list length. Kadane condition explanations are expanded to five substeps, including the reason for moving to the next line. General condition explanations are similarly enhanced to include the same five substeps. The user interface now gracefully renders general conditions, showing the actual code branch and a True/False indicator.\n\n\nFocusing on adding comprehensive support for `while` loops within the explanation structure. This involves detailed substeps for condition evaluation, execution flow, and iteration control within `explainer.js`.  For `for` loops, ensuring each substep clearly explains iteration and variable assignments. Variable changes, distinguishing creation from update, and explaining memory binding are critical. The augmented assignment operator symbol is dynamically derived, for improved clarity.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js\"","EndLine":"1240","StartLine":"1110","toolAction":"\"Viewing lines 1110 to 1240 in explainer.js\"","toolSummary":"\"View explainer.js lines 1110 to 1240\""}}]}
